%   program in the machine translated it into the machine's own "internal
%   form".  That is what a deck means by assembler, and the earliest full
%   published description of such a scheme is Wilkes, Wheeler and Gill's
%   1951 book, the first book on programming.
% FOUND-VIA: known-item verification, not discovery.  (1) Existence and
%   metadata: WebSearch '"Preparation of Programs for an Electronic Digital
%   Computer" Wilkes Wheeler Gill 1951 scan pdf full text archive', which
%   located the Internet Archive item programsforelect00wilk; metadata
