%   -- the item's own OCR of the 1951 printing, read locally (535 kB).
%   The book is a trade monograph with no DOI, hence no doi field.
% PICKED: the primary source itself, and the one the module can point a
%   student at.  Wheeler's Proc. Roy. Soc. paper (Wheeler1950InitialOrders)
%   is earlier and is the initial orders' own publication, but it was not
%   obtainable in full text; the book is both obtainable and the fuller
%   description, and it is the work the historical literature treats as the
%   founding text of programming.
% QUOTE (sec. 2-3, p. 26): "The form in which orders are written and punched
%   on the input tape differs from the form they take in the store of the
%   machine.  The written and punched form is called the external form, and
%   the form inside the machine the internal form.  Conversion from the
%   external to the internal form takes place automatically, in a way which
%   will be described later, when the input tape is read by the machine."
